    "effect": "none"
   },
   "intro": "Turn {stranding:turns}. {stranding:kept} of six jobs held. The whole beach is holding its breath.\n\n*The tide lifts it. It rolls once. It goes.*\n\nIt leaves a trench the shape of a Wailord, and a town of people sitting down in the wet sand, laughing and shaking.",
   "choices": [
    {
     "label": "Watch it go.",
     "success": {
      "text": "Out past the harbour wall, a spout goes up, and keeps going up. Captain Ffion takes off her cap and doesn't put it back.\n\nBehind the party's boat, something small and round surfaces. A Wailmer. It follows you all the way to the dock.\n\n\"The next crossing,\" Ffion says, \"the harbour'll shave a step off. A boat's a small thing to give. It's what we've got.\"",
      "effects": [
       {
        "kind": "join",
        "shadow": false,
        "species": [
         "wailmer"
        ],
        "types": [],
        "levelBonus": 0,
